                        "glosses": [
                            "Perception, information sensorielle que notre esprit traduit en concepts."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c1842f5f-f115-3901-9556-2a2e3620bc96",
                        "entry_id": "33678766-6f90-3247-884d-6534335caf76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Perception, information sensorielle que notre esprit traduit en concepts."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f259dad-e0c9-40ca-9bcf-b66669a46534",
                                "sense_id": "c1842f5f-f115-3901-9556-2a2e3620bc96",
                                "text": "Nous paierons une attachée de presse pour pouvoir dire dans les pages communication de Stratégies que : « Il faut bien distinguer le concept du percept. »"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eab16f60-6243-430e-8c1b-306382617814",
                                "sense_id": "c1842f5f-f115-3901-9556-2a2e3620bc96",
                                "text": "L’amygdale […] que la neurologie clinique a depuis longtemps identifiée comme étant l’une des clés de voûte de notre faculté à attribuer une coloration émotionnelle à nos pensées et à nos percepts les plus divers. — (Lionel Naccache, Le Nouvel Inconscient : Freud, le Christophe Colomb des neurosciences, Odile Jacob, 2009, page 38)"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3d84e60-5f04-392f-a935-47ecc08db684",
                        "entry_id": "33678766-6f90-3247-884d-6534335caf76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Perception, information sensorielle que notre esprit traduit en concepts."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ingénierie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "799823bc-c421-4d75-9c4d-8fb2d6f5d40f",
                                "sense_id": "d3d84e60-5f04-392f-a935-47ecc08db684",
                                "text": "On emploie le terme de percept pour désigner le contenu perçu par les capteurs d'un agent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fc98a603-eb3e-46f8-9662-aa2b8424de89",
                        "source_entry_id": "33678766-6f90-3247-884d-6534335caf76",
                        "target_lang_word": "percept",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "percept",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e8a05a8f-eacb-3a09-bd95-c1dac780d6f1",
                                        "entry_id": "63788f31-7874-3447-add4-3db168e8b411",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something perceived; the object of perception."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de413199-36d5-41bb-b22d-969db070e3e5",
                                                "sense_id": "e8a05a8f-eacb-3a09-bd95-c1dac780d6f1",
                                                "text": "Whether it might not, in like manner, be proper to introduce the term percept for the object of perception, I shall not at present inquire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "82b815db-1745-3c83-848d-ed0ea518714e",
                                        "entry_id": "63788f31-7874-3447-add4-3db168e8b411",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A perceived object as it exists in the mind of someone perceiving it; the mental impression that is the result of perceiving something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3984a920-9675-47f5-b84c-5ab72cf482e7",
                                                "sense_id": "82b815db-1745-3c83-848d-ed0ea518714e",
                                                "text": "I see an inkstand on the table: that is a percept. Moving my head, I get a different percept of the inkstand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04772d37-08f7-4865-9c45-f3cf75cbaddf",
                                                "sense_id": "82b815db-1745-3c83-848d-ed0ea518714e",
                                                "text": "So far as in that world it is a stable feature, holds ink, marks paper and obeys the guidance of a hand, it is a physical pen. [...] So far as it is instable, on the contrary, coming and going with the movements of my eyes, altering with what I call my fancy, continuous with subsequent experiences of its ‘having been’ (in the past tense), it is the percept of a pen in my mind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71a94da8-9fdd-4c4c-91be-310caac79240",
                                                "sense_id": "82b815db-1745-3c83-848d-ed0ea518714e",
                                                "text": "Socrates remarks that when he is well he finds wine sweet, but when ill, sour. Here it is a change in the percipient that causes the change in the percept."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "percept",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74dff17f-a2eb-3858-875f-bb76645b9d3f",
                                        "entry_id": "173314ad-c702-3b71-a97a-667aea4e9673",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "to perceive"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8c92069-2667-4f00-b62a-d25be72476b0",
                                                "sense_id": "74dff17f-a2eb-3858-875f-bb76645b9d3f",
                                                "text": "And is not the highest speculation of it percepted and perfected by manuall instruments, and those fallacious too, as themselves complain?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
